# The gate's own footprint. This is the recipe in PLUNK-IN.md step 3, plus the
# JSONFuzz-specific rules. The C++ gate's `tree` stage fails when the gate's own
# output shows up as an untracked file, so these are ignored BEFORE the first run.

# the gate's own footprint
.ci-logs/
build/
build-*/
.ci.env

# python
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# deno
# (nothing: deno.lock belongs in git)

# defensive, beyond the shipped recipe
_deps/
*.log

# JSONFuzz-specific
# fuzz/corpus/ is scratch (libFuzzer grows it); fuzz/seeds/ and fuzz/regressions/
# are TRACKED (the seeds are the documentation examples, a defect found becomes a
# tracked reproducer).
fuzz/corpus/
# the CLI `gen --intent <file>` sidecar
*.intent.json

# NOT ignored, deliberately: .ci/ holds the clang-tidy baseline
# (.ci/tidy-baseline.txt), which is tracked — it is this repo's accepted-findings list
# and the tidy stage compares against it. Ignoring the directory would silently exempt
# that file from the tree stage, which is the failure the stage exists to catch.
